WEBVTT

00:03:59.059 --> 00:04:03.996
Now, you're all going to consume the tea.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.059
So imagine that you're taking the tea now,

00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:07.863
we'll wait for you to finish the tea.

00:04:07.887 --> 00:04:11.743
We'll give another five minutes
for the ingredient to have its effects.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:16.551
Now you're going to have
30 minutes to solve 15 puzzles.

00:04:17.328 --> 00:04:19.929
Here's an example of the puzzle
you're going to solve.

00:04:20.645 --> 00:04:22.738
Anyone in the audience
want to take a stab?

00:04:22.762 --> 00:04:24.923
Audience member: Pulpit!
Baba Shiv: Whoa! OK.

00:04:24.947 --> 00:04:26.097
That's cool.

00:04:26.121 --> 00:04:29.125
Yeah, so what we'd do if we had
you who gave the answer

00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:30.428
as a participant,